# Smart Warehouse and Inventory Management System

## Project Synopsis

The Smart Warehouse and Inventory Management System is a Data
Structures and Algorithms based project developed in C. The system
is designed to manage product information and demonstrate the
practical application of various data structures and algorithms.

The project uses linked lists for product management, stacks for
undo/redo operations, queues for warehouse processing, binary
search trees for organized product storage, and graphs for
representing warehouse relationships.

## Objectives

- Manage product information efficiently
- Demonstrate Linked List operations
- Implement Stack and Queue
- Implement Binary Search Tree
- Perform BFS and DFS
- Implement searching and sorting algorithms
- Compare algorithm performance

## Technologies Used

- C Programming
- Data Structures and Algorithms
- VS Code

## Project Features

- Add, delete and search products
- Display product inventory
- Undo/Redo operations
- Product searching
- Sorting products
- BFS and DFS traversal
- Binary tree traversal



