The Smart Warehouse and Inventory Management System demonstrates how fundamental Data Structures and Algorithms can be
applied to a practical warehouse environment. By combining linked lists, stacks, queues, trees, graphs, searching, sorting,
Dynamic Programming, and Greedy algorithms, the system provides a comprehensive demonstration of DSA concepts in C.

The project is therefore not simply an inventory application; it is a practical DSA model that maps individual
data structures and algorithms to real-world warehouse operations such as inventory organization, order processing, 
route planning, and cargo optimization.









